   D. Pending-clear helper

   File:

   ```text
   board/bk7258_t5ai/chip/bk7258_irq.c
   ```

   Added helper:

   ```c
   void bk7258_clear_pending_irq(int irq)
   {
     unsigned int external;

     DEBUGASSERT(irq >= BK7258_IRQ_FIRST && irq < NR_IRQS);

     if (irq < BK7258_IRQ_FIRST || irq >= NR_IRQS)
       {
         return;
       }

     external = (unsigned int)(irq - BK7258_IRQ_FIRST);
     putreg32(1u << (external & 0x1f),
              NVIC_IRQ_CLRPEND(external));
     UP_DSB();
     UP_ISB();
   }
   ```

   `up_prioritize_irq()` writes a raw eight-bit priority field:

   ```c
   regval &= ~(0xff << shift);
   regval |= (priority << shift);
   ```

   Therefore the bridge correctly passes `0x00` or `0xc0`, not logical `0` or `6`.

